# Full Project Refactor & Behavioral Intelligence Platform MVP

This plan outlines the refactoring of the Coadex 2.0 interview integrity platform into a clean, modular, and GitHub-ready structure, as well as the implementation of the intelligent DNS enrichment pipeline.

## Proposed Changes

### Core Backend & Orchestration
Separate the project into clear modules: [api/](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/dns_event_detector.py#254-285), `dns_monitor/`, [enrichment/](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/domain_intelligence_db.py#207-247), [intelligence/](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/domain_intelligence_db.py#405-473), and `anomaly_engine/`.

#### [NEW] [Refactored Structure]
- `backend/`
    - [api/](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/dns_event_detector.py#254-285): FastAPI endpoints (session management, events).
    - `dns_monitor/`: DNS capture (PyShark) and logging.
    - [enrichment/](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/domain_intelligence_db.py#207-247): Rule-based categorization + Sarvam-2B integration.
    - [intelligence/](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/domain_intelligence_db.py#405-473): SQLite domain cache and reporting.
    - `anomaly_engine/`: Behavioral detection logic.

### Module Improvements
- **[dns_capture.py](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/dns_capture.py)**: Fix root privilege handling and ensure clean shutdown.
- **[domain_intelligence_db.py](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/domain_intelligence_db.py)**: Consolidate SQLite usage and add migration support if schemas change.
- **[Sarvam_enrichment.py](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/Sarvam_enrichment.py)**: Correct API endpoints and improve error handling for rate limits.
- **[monitor_v3.py](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/monitor_v3.py)**: Clean up orchestrator logic to remove direct Pyshark imports in the class initializer.

### Deployment & Documentation
- **`setup.sh`**: Automate tshark and dependencies installation on Ubuntu.
- **`README.md`**: Comprehensive documentation for architecture and deployment.
- **[requirements.txt](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/ec2_backend/requirements.txt)**: Unified dependencies.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- `pytest`: I will add a `tests/` directory to verify:
    - Rule-based categorization accuracy.
    - SQLite storage and retrieval (Mocked).
    - Sarvam API payload structure.

### Manual Verification
1. Run `setup.sh` in a simulated Ubuntu environment (if possible) or verify commands.
2. Launch [monitor_v3.py](file:///c:/Users/mohap/OneDrive/Desktop/Coadex%202_0/Instance_work/monitor_v3.py) and verify real-time categorization of domains like `google.com` and `openai.com`.
3. Check `dns_logs/` for structured JSON and SQLite output.
